1
00:00:01,060 --> 00:00:06,050
<i>If the red string of fate 
ties two people together,</i>

2
00:00:06,730 --> 00:00:11,560
<i>what color string connects
two unrequited lovers?</i>

3
00:00:12,660 --> 00:00:14,670
<i>"That stuff doesn't exist," you say?</i>

4
00:00:15,450 --> 00:00:16,730
<i>Of course it does.</i>

5
00:00:16,370 --> 00:00:24,330
Beautiful Meanings
Behind Flowers

6
00:00:17,860 --> 00:00:20,080
<i>How else could two people 
have such a strong bond</i>

7
00:00:20,510 --> 00:00:23,180
<i>but be destined to be apart?</i>

8
00:00:24,350 --> 00:00:28,040
<i>I bet it's a string with a lame color.</i>

9
00:00:29,310 --> 00:00:32,890
<i>Like the color of my eyes right now.</i>

10
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:34,400
<i>I'm sure of it.</i>

11
00:00:35,340 --> 00:00:39,140
Flowers that Bloom Along
 the Path of Dreams

12
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:41,040
<i>I really hate the summer.</i>

13
00:00:41,250 --> 00:00:42,440
<i>I sweat way too much.</i>

14
00:00:42,440 --> 00:00:44,730
<i>And guys stare more.</i>

15
00:00:51,610 --> 00:00:54,160
<i>We don't have band practice today but...</i>

16
00:00:54,480 --> 00:00:56,570
<i>I bet Yu-kun doesn't want any visitors.</i>

17
00:00:56,570 --> 00:00:58,920
Rion! Got a minute?

18
00:00:59,670 --> 00:01:03,120
Can you take Kureha's gift 
to the Makishimas?

19
00:01:04,030 --> 00:01:05,580
But it's my day off!

20
00:01:06,170 --> 00:01:07,800
Can't Onee-chan take it?

21
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:09,630
Looks like she's already left.

22
00:01:09,630 --> 00:01:10,580
What?

23
00:01:10,750 --> 00:01:13,560
You know how restless she gets.

24
00:01:13,880 --> 00:01:15,160
Thanks, Rion.

25
00:01:16,520 --> 00:01:19,960
You're way too soft on Onee-chan.

26
00:01:25,350 --> 00:01:27,780
It's done! Himari-chan's going to Tokyo!

27
00:01:27,780 --> 00:01:30,600
Rin-chan's sure to win now!

28
00:01:30,880 --> 00:01:35,000
That lame perfectionist's got nothing on me!

29
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:36,560
Take that, you loser!

30
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:39,440
<i>He's weirdly energetic, it's creepy.</i>

31
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:41,980
You're home for a change?

32
00:01:42,380 --> 00:01:44,600
I figured you'd be out with girls.

33
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:49,340
I'm in a good mood. Don't burst my bubble.

34
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:51,020
What's the visit for?

35
00:01:52,270 --> 00:01:54,690
Oh, Kureha-san's gift.

36
00:01:54,690 --> 00:01:57,000
I'll give it to the others later.

37
00:01:59,250 --> 00:02:00,240
What's your problem?

38
00:02:00,240 --> 00:02:02,140
Go ahead and say it.

39
00:02:02,420 --> 00:02:05,790
Onee-chan's trying to take Hii-chan away.

40
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:09,820
She seems pretty set on her.

41
00:02:10,330 --> 00:02:12,890
But this is your chance, isn't it?

42
00:02:13,110 --> 00:02:14,610
That's not fair, though.

43
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:17,760
You're still trying to play nice?

44
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:20,540
Himari-chan was the one 
who tried to one-up you.

45
00:02:20,540 --> 00:02:22,200
Anything's fair game.

46
00:02:22,850 --> 00:02:24,430
I mean sure, but...

47
00:02:25,170 --> 00:02:27,240
Shii-kun, can you stop her?

48
00:02:27,630 --> 00:02:29,250
No can do.

49
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:33,170
I've pulled all these strings 
to help you win.

50
00:02:33,170 --> 00:02:34,520
I can't put all my hard work to wast—

51
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:39,610
I bet Onee-chan would be impressed 
if you can outsmart her.

52
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:43,760
Like with tennis.

53
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:49,800
Going to nationals is just to make 
Onee-chan admit you're above Hibari-san.

54
00:02:50,380 --> 00:02:55,560
Not to mention you only approached Yu-kun
because he was Hibari-san's favorite.

55
00:02:56,120 --> 00:02:58,590
And now look at you, you're actual friends.

56
00:02:58,590 --> 00:02:59,990
Want me to keep going?

57
00:03:05,700 --> 00:03:07,320
Fine! I get it!

58
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:08,790
You're right.

59
00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:13,480
Not that I care one bit about 
that cruel woman!

60
00:03:13,930 --> 00:03:16,880
But it would feel nice 
to beat her at her own game.

61
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:18,590
You sure, though?

62
00:03:18,590 --> 00:03:22,880
You might essentially be handing 
the win to Himari-chan!

63
00:03:22,880 --> 00:03:23,660
Fine with me!

64
00:03:24,010 --> 00:03:26,360
I don't want to win like this anyways.

65
00:03:26,670 --> 00:03:29,950
You sisters are both so stubborn.

66
00:03:30,380 --> 00:03:33,470
Fine, but after this, 
I'm not helping you anymore.

67
00:03:33,470 --> 00:03:34,440
Got that?

68
00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:38,070
I never asked you for help. Besides...

69
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:40,860
I'm only letting Himari-chan borrow Yu-kun.

70
00:03:41,640 --> 00:03:43,770
In the end, I'll be the winner!

71
00:03:45,870 --> 00:03:46,740
Good grief.

72
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:51,830
I almost feel bad for Himari-chan for having

73
00:03:51,830 --> 00:03:53,710
a lifelong rival with such nerves of steel.

74
00:04:01,090 --> 00:04:02,460
Hi, there.

75
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:04,690
What an unexpected caller.

76
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:06,860
A favor?

77
00:04:10,490 --> 00:04:14,970
<i>I'll be all alone at the 
Gardening Club until graduation.</i>

78
00:04:16,120 --> 00:04:19,030
<i>It might even be that way 
until I open my own store.</i>

79
00:04:19,640 --> 00:04:21,880
<i>Or even for the rest of my life.</i>

80
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:25,230
<i>Himari may never come back.</i>

81
00:04:25,960 --> 00:04:29,100
<i>If it comes to that, would 
I even want to open a store?</i>

82
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:34,230
<i>I'd spend ten, twenty years living 
an ordinary life without her.</i>

83
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:37,640
<i>Dammit!</i>

84
00:04:37,640 --> 00:04:39,880
<i>Why am I being so negative?!</i>

85
00:04:40,760 --> 00:04:41,790
<i>Everything will be fine!</i>

86
00:04:41,790 --> 00:04:44,300
<i>I trust Himari. I'll work hard, too!</i>

87
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:49,290
You look as miserable as ever.

88
00:04:49,290 --> 00:04:52,680
Isn't it Himari-chan's job to water 
the flowers in the morning?

89
00:04:53,070 --> 00:04:54,880
She's leaving for Tokyo today.

90
00:04:55,130 --> 00:04:56,400
What time does the train leave?

91
00:04:56,780 --> 00:04:58,010
Around noon, I think.

92
00:04:58,010 --> 00:05:00,120
Then we've got some time.

93
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:01,130
Let's have a chat.

94
00:05:01,130 --> 00:05:01,870
Huh?

95
00:05:01,870 --> 00:05:04,920
You're going too, aren't you?

96
00:05:04,920 --> 00:05:07,270
This might be our last chance 
to talk face-to-face.

97
00:05:07,270 --> 00:05:09,330
Why would I go to Tokyo?

98
00:05:09,330 --> 00:05:10,040
Oh?

99
00:05:10,330 --> 00:05:14,330
Weren't you all worked up 
about following her back in May?

100
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:17,990
You've already decided 
to give up accessories once.

101
00:05:17,990 --> 00:05:19,710
How's it different 
the second or third time?

102
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:22,730
This situation's totally different.

103
00:05:22,730 --> 00:05:24,050
Is it? How so?

104
00:05:24,050 --> 00:05:27,570
Himari wants to model for my accessories.

105
00:05:27,570 --> 00:05:29,090
How could I stop her?

106
00:05:29,090 --> 00:05:29,720
How lame.

107
00:05:30,150 --> 00:05:31,780
That's how I know you're stupid.

108
00:05:32,310 --> 00:05:33,320
What do you—

109
00:05:34,690 --> 00:05:37,290
What's so wrong about 
devoting your life to a woman?

110
00:05:37,560 --> 00:05:41,480
You don't need your own store 
to make accessories.

111
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:44,860
You don't have to be an artist,
you can work a normal job

112
00:05:44,860 --> 00:05:46,620
and be with the woman you love.

113
00:05:46,620 --> 00:05:49,020
Is that such a bad life?

114
00:05:49,540 --> 00:05:52,210
But you can't make that choice.

115
00:05:52,930 --> 00:05:56,560
Why? Because you're afraid of going 
back to your old, boring self.

116
00:05:56,560 --> 00:06:00,420
You're afraid of being surrounded 
by people who look down on you.

117
00:06:02,220 --> 00:06:03,470
Let me be brutally honest.

118
00:06:03,870 --> 00:06:06,940
You don't actually love Himari-chan.

119
00:06:07,450 --> 00:06:09,170
You're just taking advantage of her.

120
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:15,360
You spent two years as her best friend
only because that's what she wanted.

121
00:06:15,640 --> 00:06:18,600
Now that she wants romance, 
you're playing your part.

122
00:06:19,810 --> 00:06:22,260
It's all for your own convenience.

123
00:06:22,260 --> 00:06:24,270
You wouldn't care whichever way.

124
00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:28,860
What the hell would you know?

125
00:06:28,860 --> 00:06:29,690
You—!

126
00:06:30,320 --> 00:06:32,440
You have no clue 
what we mean to each other!

127
00:06:32,810 --> 00:06:35,840
I... I love Himari!

128
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:38,330
Even if she didn't help my dream!

129
00:06:38,330 --> 00:06:40,720
Even if she didn't protect me!

130
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:43,150
I've already decided to be with Himari!

131
00:06:44,640 --> 00:06:46,920
Great. You know where you stand.

132
00:06:47,840 --> 00:06:50,550
Now there's only one thing to do.

133
00:06:55,570 --> 00:06:57,820
I played it close, he almost hit me.

134
00:07:01,440 --> 00:07:07,720
It's not easy having to live 
without your number one girl like me.

135
00:07:17,270 --> 00:07:20,240
<i>That's right. It was her all along.</i>

136
00:07:21,100 --> 00:07:23,710
<i>I just wanted her eyes on me.</i>

137
00:07:35,270 --> 00:07:36,310
Whoa, bro.

138
00:07:37,140 --> 00:07:38,270
You okay?

139
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:50,620
Yu!

140
00:08:01,280 --> 00:08:03,980
<i>That's all I needed!</i>

141
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:16,040
<i>I'm such a backstabber.</i>

142
00:08:16,830 --> 00:08:18,920
<i>I pretended to support Enocchi.</i>

143
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:21,440
<i>Only to kiss Yu behind her back.</i>

144
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:28,600
<i>But... I've never liked someone so much</i>

145
00:08:29,300 --> 00:08:31,240
<i>that none of that even mattered.</i>

146
00:08:33,820 --> 00:08:37,490
On my way!

147
00:08:33,820 --> 00:08:37,490
I'm by the station entrance.

148
00:08:33,820 --> 00:08:37,490
Oops, sorry. Stuck in traffic.

149
00:08:35,330 --> 00:08:37,480
<i>I hope she doesn't show up.</i>

150
00:08:38,570 --> 00:08:41,240
<i>Snap out of it. You've made up your mind.</i>

151
00:08:42,310 --> 00:08:43,750
<i>I was just unlucky.</i>

152
00:08:45,130 --> 00:08:48,910
<i>Kureha-san said my looks were my talent.</i>

153
00:08:49,460 --> 00:08:51,920
<i>That made me happy.</i>

154
00:08:52,780 --> 00:08:55,860
<i>After all, I didn't think 
I was good for anything.</i>

155
00:08:56,560 --> 00:08:59,060
<i>Maybe, just maybe, my looks could help Yu.</i>

156
00:09:00,590 --> 00:09:05,450
<i>Still, if I think about 
what's most important to me,</i>

157
00:09:06,210 --> 00:09:07,650
<i>it's the time I spend with Yu.</i>

158
00:09:08,080 --> 00:09:10,390
<i>And now, I can't have that anymore.</i>

159
00:09:11,820 --> 00:09:16,300
<i>If that's how it is, I don't want to 
be the prettiest girl in the world.</i>

160
00:09:16,680 --> 00:09:19,350
<i>I don't even want these fairy-like eyes.</i>

161
00:09:19,830 --> 00:09:22,190
<i>Or any friends. Or family.</i>

162
00:09:24,160 --> 00:09:28,120
<i>I just wish I were born 
as someone loved by Yu.</i>

163
00:09:30,910 --> 00:09:31,500
Hii-chan.

164
00:09:32,960 --> 00:09:34,200
E-Enocchi!

165
00:09:34,200 --> 00:09:35,520
You came to see me off?

166
00:09:36,610 --> 00:09:38,390
You're too nice!

167
00:09:38,910 --> 00:09:41,730
Not like that idiot who left me on read.

168
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:43,220
I'm not here for that.

169
00:09:43,670 --> 00:09:44,840
I just wanted to say thanks.

170
00:09:45,350 --> 00:09:46,080
Say thanks?

171
00:09:46,410 --> 00:09:48,850
Hii-chan, you threw the match.

172
00:09:49,400 --> 00:09:50,110
So thanks!

173
00:09:53,510 --> 00:09:56,600
Y-You're mad I kissed Yu, huh?

174
00:09:56,600 --> 00:09:58,000
That was nothing, it was—

175
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:00,760
You're still trying to play the good girl?

176
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:04,650
It's been obvious the entire time.

177
00:10:04,960 --> 00:10:06,630
There's no use glossing it over.

178
00:10:08,160 --> 00:10:13,080
Are your dreams more important 
than your true feelings?

179
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:14,750
O-Of course they are!

180
00:10:14,750 --> 00:10:18,170
You know how hard Yu's worked for it!

181
00:10:18,170 --> 00:10:19,510
Sure I do.

182
00:10:19,760 --> 00:10:22,790
It would be a huge plus 
for the store one day.

183
00:10:22,790 --> 00:10:26,410
Besides, modeling 
isn't something anyone can do.

184
00:10:26,980 --> 00:10:30,480
But why do it if you don't want to?

185
00:10:30,480 --> 00:10:32,730
Then why don't you go instead!

186
00:10:38,180 --> 00:10:38,730
Okay!

187
00:10:40,800 --> 00:10:41,590
I'll go.

188
00:10:42,150 --> 00:10:46,610
I'm not sure if I'm cut out for it, 
but I'll do it for you and Yu-kun.

189
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:48,700
B-But...

190
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:51,540
So give me Yu-kun in return.

191
00:10:52,820 --> 00:10:55,630
I'll let you borrow him 
until he opens his store.

192
00:10:56,160 --> 00:10:59,050
But when I come home, give him to me.

193
00:10:59,750 --> 00:11:00,470
You don't mind, right?

194
00:11:00,470 --> 00:11:01,970
Let's pinky promise!

195
00:11:03,490 --> 00:11:04,300
No?

196
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:06,530
You can still be best friends.

197
00:11:06,800 --> 00:11:08,030
It's okay.

198
00:11:08,030 --> 00:11:11,400
I'm sure you'll be able to 
find someone just like him!

199
00:11:12,370 --> 00:11:14,980
<i>No, that's not it.</i>

200
00:11:16,160 --> 00:11:18,460
<i>I wasn't the one who found Yu.</i>

201
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:23,000
<i>Yu was the one who discovered me.</i>

202
00:11:23,320 --> 00:11:24,990
<i>There's no doing that again.</i>

203
00:11:29,830 --> 00:11:32,440
See, you're trying too hard.

204
00:11:33,910 --> 00:11:35,950
You've always been like that.

205
00:11:36,290 --> 00:11:39,880
Even though you steal everything you want,

206
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:45,030
you've never been able to 
say what you want most.

207
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:54,500
I don't wanna!

208
00:11:55,370 --> 00:11:56,780
I hate it!

209
00:11:57,190 --> 00:11:59,650
I don't really wanna go!

210
00:12:00,240 --> 00:12:02,860
There, there. I know.

211
00:12:03,840 --> 00:12:05,830
But this was all my fault.

212
00:12:05,830 --> 00:12:07,890
I have to make up for it somehow.

213
00:12:08,090 --> 00:12:12,150
And what if Yu's better off without me?

214
00:12:12,150 --> 00:12:14,600
Honestly, I wonder about that too.

215
00:12:14,840 --> 00:12:19,330
You always stir up trouble
and involve everyone around you.

216
00:12:19,330 --> 00:12:22,690
Are you trying to kill me or what?

217
00:12:25,790 --> 00:12:27,470
You know what I noticed?

218
00:12:27,920 --> 00:12:33,440
You two are both so focused on 
how to make your dreams come true.

219
00:12:33,440 --> 00:12:34,720
What do you mean?

220
00:12:34,720 --> 00:12:36,810
Does it have to be that complicated?

221
00:12:37,180 --> 00:12:38,430
Like my mom.

222
00:12:38,430 --> 00:12:41,030
Making sweets was initially just a hobby.

223
00:12:41,030 --> 00:12:42,880
She only opened her own store recently.

224
00:12:42,880 --> 00:12:43,990
Really?

225
00:12:44,510 --> 00:12:48,370
Having a dream is nice, but you 
can't lose sight of the present.

226
00:12:48,890 --> 00:12:50,800
Opening a store isn't everything.

227
00:12:51,420 --> 00:12:53,180
But it might be for Yu.

228
00:12:54,900 --> 00:12:56,360
You think so?

229
00:12:56,360 --> 00:13:00,590
Is the store the most 
important thing to Yu-kun?

230
00:13:01,270 --> 00:13:02,290
Or is it—

231
00:13:02,290 --> 00:13:03,300
Himari!

232
00:13:04,530 --> 00:13:05,510
Himari!

233
00:13:10,550 --> 00:13:11,350
Yu!

234
00:13:13,220 --> 00:13:14,060
See?

235
00:13:14,850 --> 00:13:16,580
What are you doing here?

236
00:13:16,580 --> 00:13:18,270
Please don't go!

237
00:13:18,550 --> 00:13:21,160
I can't choose between 
my dream and romance.

238
00:13:21,160 --> 00:13:23,560
I'm not even sure which is the right answer.

239
00:13:23,560 --> 00:13:27,700
But I <i>do</i> know that you don't 
actually want to go to Tokyo!

240
00:13:28,130 --> 00:13:32,150
But this is the only way I can help.

241
00:13:32,550 --> 00:13:33,610
That's not true.

242
00:13:34,190 --> 00:13:36,630
And you don't need to help me.

243
00:13:37,460 --> 00:13:40,070
You don't need to do anything.

244
00:13:40,070 --> 00:13:41,690
We don't need a purpose to be together.

245
00:13:41,690 --> 00:13:43,330
That's not what this is about!

246
00:13:44,210 --> 00:13:48,040
I was so afraid to lose the one
 person who understands my passion.

247
00:13:48,610 --> 00:13:50,960
I was too afraid to lose you!

248
00:13:51,740 --> 00:13:54,600
That's why I was so fixated 
on what we could do for each other.

249
00:13:54,840 --> 00:13:59,810
But all I ever wanted was for you to see me!

250
00:14:00,560 --> 00:14:03,770
If you're doing this for me, 
don't sacrifice yourself!

251
00:14:04,210 --> 00:14:06,720
There's no having fun without you around.

252
00:14:07,160 --> 00:14:10,140
Like the best friends we've always been!

253
00:14:13,560 --> 00:14:15,700
Yu, I—

254
00:14:17,390 --> 00:14:19,660
All right you two, that's enough.

255
00:14:20,120 --> 00:14:23,640
Yu-chan, I'm not sure that's very fair.

256
00:14:23,640 --> 00:14:25,670
You lost the match, remember?

257
00:14:26,030 --> 00:14:28,130
Kureha-san, I can't go!

258
00:14:28,430 --> 00:14:31,490
Please, give us one more chance!

259
00:14:31,490 --> 00:14:32,640
Nope, sorry.

260
00:14:32,640 --> 00:14:36,390
I only gave you the first chance 
for Hibari-kun's sake.

261
00:14:36,390 --> 00:14:39,760
Besides, aren't you two 
forgetting something?

262
00:14:40,590 --> 00:14:43,890
Himari-chan has a debt to pay.

263
00:14:43,890 --> 00:14:45,780
First thing's first, she should—

264
00:14:45,780 --> 00:14:48,520
Then allow <i>me</i> to pay that off!

265
00:14:52,270 --> 00:14:53,540
Here you go!

266
00:14:53,540 --> 00:14:54,910
Wh-What's going on?

267
00:14:57,540 --> 00:14:59,080
Ouch...

268
00:14:59,430 --> 00:15:02,540
What's all this about?

269
00:15:02,540 --> 00:15:04,200
Shii-kun, you're late.

270
00:15:05,970 --> 00:15:07,350
Well it was a lot of cash.

271
00:15:08,140 --> 00:15:09,850
Though, I will say,

272
00:15:09,850 --> 00:15:12,620
hats off to that perfectionist 
for making it in time.

273
00:15:16,550 --> 00:15:17,550
Onii-chan!

274
00:15:17,960 --> 00:15:20,760
Shinji-kun, you better explain yourself.

275
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:25,110
Like I said, I'm paying off 
Himari-chan's debt on her behalf.

276
00:15:25,440 --> 00:15:29,900
As an outsider, I can sign a contract 
with Hibari-san to borrow money.

277
00:15:31,620 --> 00:15:34,160
I didn't expect you 
to betray me of all people.

278
00:15:34,160 --> 00:15:38,590
Betray you? Please. You declined my offer.

279
00:15:38,830 --> 00:15:42,120
Did you expect me to sit idly by?

280
00:15:42,120 --> 00:15:44,170
You can't be that naive.

281
00:15:44,500 --> 00:15:47,090
Well? You've got your money.

282
00:15:47,090 --> 00:15:48,720
Any other problems?

283
00:15:56,920 --> 00:15:57,390
I—

284
00:15:57,390 --> 00:15:58,840
I'm over this!

285
00:15:59,130 --> 00:16:01,430
Huh? Wait, um...

286
00:16:03,520 --> 00:16:06,030
Thanks for ruining everything.

287
00:16:07,310 --> 00:16:08,520
Hey now! Kureha-kun!

288
00:16:08,520 --> 00:16:09,610
Stop that!

289
00:16:09,610 --> 00:16:14,240
Hurry up and take me somewhere 
cool so I can let you have it!

290
00:16:14,930 --> 00:16:17,160
It's always this with you!

291
00:16:17,620 --> 00:16:19,560
That's that. You can go now.

292
00:16:19,560 --> 00:16:20,730
Bye-bye!

293
00:16:25,240 --> 00:16:27,490
Are we off the hook?

294
00:16:27,490 --> 00:16:28,920
I dunno, maybe?

295
00:16:28,920 --> 00:16:31,120
According to Kureha-san, it was a loan.

296
00:16:31,120 --> 00:16:33,000
Pay it off and it's a done deal.

297
00:16:33,420 --> 00:16:39,630
Good thing I bought Natsu, Himari-chan, 
and Rin-chan's entire high school years!

298
00:16:41,690 --> 00:16:44,220
From now on, no quitting school 
or going to Tokyo.

299
00:16:44,220 --> 00:16:46,380
I won't allow it!

300
00:16:46,380 --> 00:16:50,320
Of course, you'll also be forced 
to make accessories until we graduate.

301
00:16:50,520 --> 00:16:53,420
Stay tuned for other arrangements to follow.

302
00:16:53,590 --> 00:16:57,120
Makishima-kun, you really are the worst.

303
00:16:57,120 --> 00:16:59,670
I like to keep myself amused.

304
00:16:59,670 --> 00:17:03,160
You three's rom-com does the trick.

305
00:17:04,160 --> 00:17:07,000
Nothing wrong with paying 
for a little entertainment.

306
00:17:09,440 --> 00:17:10,400
Never mind that.

307
00:17:10,400 --> 00:17:13,180
Now that things are settled, let's go out.

308
00:17:13,720 --> 00:17:15,480
It'll be on Himari-chan, obviously.

309
00:17:15,480 --> 00:17:18,360
Why would <i>I</i> be paying?!

310
00:17:18,360 --> 00:17:20,680
Who do you have to thank but me?

311
00:17:20,990 --> 00:17:24,120
You can't argue with me ever again!

312
00:17:24,120 --> 00:17:26,220
Can you believe this guy, Enocchi?

313
00:17:26,220 --> 00:17:28,610
Actually, sushi sounds great right now.

314
00:17:29,610 --> 00:17:31,540
I see how it is!

315
00:17:37,520 --> 00:17:41,220
I got bailed out but 
definitely paid the price.

316
00:17:41,920 --> 00:17:45,630
You gotta admit though, it was a huge help.

317
00:17:45,990 --> 00:17:48,790
You're so soft on Makishima-kun.

318
00:17:48,790 --> 00:17:51,520
You'll end up in trouble 
if you keep hanging out with him.

319
00:17:51,520 --> 00:17:55,020
I'd say that's already happened a few times.

320
00:17:55,620 --> 00:17:59,030
See? You don't sense danger very well.

321
00:17:59,030 --> 00:18:03,140
That's why your store will need me!

322
00:18:03,140 --> 00:18:05,230
Oh yeah, about that...

323
00:18:06,090 --> 00:18:08,640
I'm thinking of abandoning that dream.

324
00:18:08,840 --> 00:18:10,470
What?! Why? Why?!

325
00:18:10,470 --> 00:18:12,980
It's not like Kureha-san's stopping us!

326
00:18:13,320 --> 00:18:16,070
Sorry, I worded that wrong.

327
00:18:16,550 --> 00:18:20,130
I meant we still have the same root problem.

328
00:18:20,710 --> 00:18:24,080
About what Sakura-san said?

329
00:18:24,330 --> 00:18:28,080
The "playground frozen in time," was it?

330
00:18:28,540 --> 00:18:29,020
Yup.

331
00:18:29,800 --> 00:18:34,070
The main issue was my 
stance towards customers.

332
00:18:34,500 --> 00:18:36,400
That's on me, too.

333
00:18:36,640 --> 00:18:39,680
No, I was the one being spoiled.

334
00:18:40,360 --> 00:18:43,810
Saku-nee-san was trying 
to tell me that all along.

335
00:18:43,810 --> 00:18:46,480
I just wasn't listening to her.

336
00:18:48,160 --> 00:18:49,640
I've been thinking, and I see it now.

337
00:18:50,200 --> 00:18:54,960
I was too fixated on opening my own store.

338
00:18:55,440 --> 00:18:58,280
Are you saying that shouldn't be our dream?

339
00:19:00,280 --> 00:19:02,050
No, that's not it.

340
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:07,410
Opening a store by the time we're thirty 
was our dream in middle school.

341
00:19:08,080 --> 00:19:11,800
But if we don't keep an open mind, 
we end up limiting ourselves.

342
00:19:12,680 --> 00:19:18,250
Being so focused on that one dream 
made me overlook the important things.

343
00:19:19,320 --> 00:19:23,960
Like how I wanted to keep flowers 
from dying back in grade school.

344
00:19:24,960 --> 00:19:29,120
Or how I wanted to share 
the beauty I saw in flowers with others.

345
00:19:30,430 --> 00:19:35,380
Saku-nee-san was upset that I forgot 
why I started in the first place.

346
00:19:37,050 --> 00:19:38,880
I'm dreaming even bigger from now on.

347
00:19:39,610 --> 00:19:42,310
Opening a store is only part of the process.

348
00:19:43,330 --> 00:19:45,230
Love, my dreams, my own store...

349
00:19:45,230 --> 00:19:48,150
Maybe it's selfish to want everything.

350
00:19:48,770 --> 00:19:52,120
But I'll become someone worthy of it all.

351
00:19:52,600 --> 00:19:54,450
From now on, I'll work harder 
than Saku-nee-san.

352
00:19:54,770 --> 00:19:56,720
I'll make sure Kureha-san 
never looks down on me.

353
00:19:56,720 --> 00:19:58,440
I won't give Hibari-san any reason to worry.

354
00:19:59,700 --> 00:20:01,990
You'll never have to 
sacrifice yourself again.

355
00:20:02,280 --> 00:20:05,680
I promise to stand on my own two feet.

356
00:20:06,730 --> 00:20:07,360
So...

357
00:20:08,960 --> 00:20:11,410
It's not enough to have you 
until I open a store.

358
00:20:11,950 --> 00:20:15,390
Will you let me be selfish 
and stand by me forever?

359
00:20:15,680 --> 00:20:20,430
Y-You're making me blush.

360
00:20:22,730 --> 00:20:24,370
Bwa-ha!

361
00:20:24,370 --> 00:20:27,440
Hey, Yu! You idiot!

362
00:20:27,440 --> 00:20:30,410
Found your weakness! 
It's straightforward confessions!

363
00:20:30,410 --> 00:20:32,300
Don't tease me like that!

364
00:20:32,300 --> 00:20:33,780
I'm an emotional mess right now!

365
00:20:33,780 --> 00:20:36,300
Stop playing it cool!

366
00:20:37,570 --> 00:20:38,990
Oh yeah, Himari.

367
00:20:39,890 --> 00:20:40,870
You forgot this.

368
00:20:42,840 --> 00:20:44,310
My best friend ring...

369
00:20:48,050 --> 00:20:52,140
Does this mean we're 
still only best friends?

370
00:20:55,280 --> 00:20:58,040
A totally unique best 
friend ring just for you.

371
00:20:59,730 --> 00:21:03,600
Oh, right. I chickened out back then.

372
00:21:04,800 --> 00:21:08,960
There's something I haven't 
told you about this ring.

373
00:21:09,730 --> 00:21:13,830
See this here? It's a purple tulip seed.

374
00:21:14,840 --> 00:21:17,260
Yeah, and...?

375
00:21:17,460 --> 00:21:19,370
You see, um...

376
00:21:25,510 --> 00:21:29,510
signifies "eternal love"

377
00:21:25,560 --> 00:21:27,530
<i>We used to be best friends...</i>

378
00:21:30,240 --> 00:21:33,260
<i>But now... we're not.</i>

379
00:21:36,860 --> 00:21:37,830
Himari!

380
00:21:38,360 --> 00:21:40,290
You're late!

381
00:21:40,290 --> 00:21:44,940
Sorry, I was up late last night 
after my shift at the family store.

382
00:21:45,590 --> 00:21:47,410
Thanks for covering for me.

383
00:21:49,080 --> 00:21:51,360
Will you give me something in return?

384
00:21:51,360 --> 00:21:52,330
Like what?

385
00:21:52,330 --> 00:21:54,140
Yu, do you love me?

386
00:21:55,940 --> 00:21:56,840
How much?

387
00:21:56,840 --> 00:21:57,920
More than anything in the world?

388
00:21:59,280 --> 00:22:01,200
M-More than anything in the world.

389
00:22:01,680 --> 00:22:03,240
Himari...

390
00:22:03,920 --> 00:22:04,750
Go on?

391
00:22:21,180 --> 00:22:21,850
I love you.

392
00:22:31,090 --> 00:22:32,640
Bwa-he-he.

393
00:22:33,170 --> 00:22:34,120
<i>What was that?</i>

394
00:22:34,120 --> 00:22:36,880
<i>Did the "Bwa-ha!" just evolve?</i>

395
00:22:36,880 --> 00:22:39,000
<i>Must be the lovey-dovey version.</i>

396
00:22:40,350 --> 00:22:43,960
<i>Himari's the cutest girl in the world
 when she doesn't hide her feelings.</i>

397
00:22:46,250 --> 00:22:47,170
Good grief.

398
00:22:47,170 --> 00:22:49,550
Getting it on early today, are we?

399
00:22:50,030 --> 00:22:52,350
Yu-kun, Hii-chan, good morning.

400
00:22:52,760 --> 00:22:54,600
M-Morning, Enomoto-san!

401
00:22:54,600 --> 00:22:57,970
You two aren't plotting 
to take Yu again, are you?!

402
00:22:57,970 --> 00:22:59,520
He's mine!

403
00:22:59,770 --> 00:23:02,960
I won't give you these with that attitude.

404
00:23:02,960 --> 00:23:03,980
Here you go, Yu-kun.

405
00:23:04,260 --> 00:23:05,370
Thanks!

406
00:23:07,210 --> 00:23:09,360
Not fair! I want some too!

407
00:23:07,850 --> 00:23:11,520
<i>Sometimes, I get to thinking.</i>

408
00:23:12,030 --> 00:23:15,220
<i>How we'll probably end up
 in a similar spot.</i>

409
00:23:16,200 --> 00:23:20,240
<i>We'll pretend to understand 
each other even though we don't.</i>

410
00:23:21,120 --> 00:23:24,280
<i>Even when we know 
to put our desires into words,</i>

411
00:23:24,650 --> 00:23:27,080
<i>our pride will sometimes get in the way.</i>

412
00:23:27,680 --> 00:23:31,520
<i>Still, we'll push forward into the future.</i>

413
00:23:32,880 --> 00:23:34,520
<i>This is our summer playground.</i>

414
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:37,420
<i>It's not over yet.</i>

